<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><span id="S5.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Benign relearning as a function of unlearning steps.</span> <math id="S5.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is shown for <span id="S5.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFDFDF;">unlearnt</span> and <span id="S5.T3.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#DCE6FA;">relearnt</span> models over unlearning steps. WR is reported for the unlearnt model. Relearning uses 600 steps on data disjoint from LKF forget/retain sets (see <a href="#A2.SS5" title="B.5 Relearning experiments ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Unlearning That Lasts: Utility-Preserving, Robust, and Almost Irreversible Forgetting in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>); the 200<sup id="S5.T3.9" class="ltx_sup">∗</sup>-step model matches <a href="#S5.T1" title="In 5 Unlearning Experiments ‣ Unlearning That Lasts: Utility-Preserving, Robust, and Almost Irreversible Forgetting in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</figcaption>
