<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A2.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Testing different styles of evaluations in our worst-case setup.</span> For the 60 epoch setup from <a href="#A4.T11" title="In D.3 LKF unlearning without paraphrases ‣ Appendix D Additional Unlearning Experiments ‣ Unlearning That Lasts: Utility-Preserving, Robust, and Almost Irreversible Forgetting in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> on the LKF dataset, we show adding additional query types like Fill-in-Blank ( <math id="A2.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{FB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{FB}</annotation></semantics></math>) and adding hints to the query (<math id="A2.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{Ht}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{Ht}</annotation></semantics></math>) do not help in enhancing our chosen worst-case evaluation
<math id="A2.T6.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{W}(\mathop{\rm max}\nolimits_{(1,2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">max</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{W}(\mathop{\rm max}\nolimits_{(1,2)})</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
