<span id="A5.F20.pic1.p7.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:407.9pt;--ltx-bg-color:#DCFFDC;">
<span id="A5.F20.pic1.p7.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">In 1950, the world was a vastly different place. Here’s a snapshot of what life was like back then: **Technology:** 1. **Television:** TV was still a relatively new medium, with only about 12% of American households owning a TV set. Popular shows like "I Love Lucy," "The Honeymooners," and "The Ed Sullivan Show" were popular. 2. **Radio:** Radio was still the primary source of entertainment, with many people listening to shows like "The Jack Benny Program" and "The Shadow." 3. **Computing:** The first commercial computers, like UNIV</span>
</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 20: </span><span id="A5.F20.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample outputs on the AlpacaEval instruction based question used for repetitiveness and Quality assessment.</span> For all unlearning methods used to unlearn the forget set of LKF, we show how the outputs look. Colored boxes depict: <span id="A5.F20.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#DCFFDC;">correct answer w.r.t GT/Query</span>, and <span id="A5.F20.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFDFDF;">answer incorrect or incomplete w.r.t GT/Query</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
